WEBVTT

00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:07.357
(OLAF JOINS IN)

00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:12.237
(CHANTING CONTINUES)

00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:24.877
We are called Northuldra.

00:00:25.037 --> 00:00:27.997
We are the people of the sun.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:33.677
I promise you
I will free this forest...

00:00:33.837 --> 00:00:35.237
and restore Arendelle.

00:00:36.557 --> 00:00:38.557
That's a pretty big promise,
Elsa.

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:39.997
(EXCITED CHATTER AND LAUGHTER)

00:00:40.277 --> 00:00:42.957
Free the Forest?
(CHUCKLES) Wow.

00:00:43.477 --> 00:00:44.477
I'm sorry.

00:00:44.557 --> 00:00:46.277
It's just, uh, some of us
were born in here,

00:00:46.357 --> 00:00:48.357
we've never even seen
a clear sky.

00:00:48.517 --> 00:00:49.637
I get it.

00:00:49.797 --> 00:00:51.557
-The name's Ryder.
-Kristoff.

00:00:51.757 --> 00:00:53.037
I heard the voice again.

00:00:53.197 --> 00:00:54.237
We need to go north.

00:00:54.397 --> 00:00:57.157
But the Earth Giants now roam
the north at night.

00:00:57.317 --> 00:00:59.157
You can leave in the morning.

00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:00.357
I'm Honeymaren.

00:01:00.557 --> 00:01:02.797
Honeymaren,
we'll do all we can.

00:01:04.277 --> 00:01:05.837
(CHILDREN GIGGLING)

00:01:06.437 --> 00:01:07.717
OLAF: Hey, let me ask you.

00:01:07.877 --> 00:01:08.957
How do you guys cope...

00:01:09.037 --> 00:01:11.197
with the ever-increasing
complexity of thought

00:01:11.277 --> 00:01:13.397
-that comes with maturity?
-(KID GRUNTS)

00:01:14.237 --> 00:01:15.877
-(GIGGLES)
-Brilliant!

00:01:15.957 --> 00:01:17.037
-Oh!
-(LAUGHS)

00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:19.197
It's so refreshing to talk
to the youth of today.

00:01:19.357 --> 00:01:20.677
Our future's in bright hands.

00:01:20.837 --> 00:01:22.117
Oh, no, no.
Don't chew that.

00:01:22.277 --> 00:01:23.997
You don't know
what I've stepped in.

00:01:24.157 --> 00:01:25.877
I can't seem
to get her attention. I can't seem
to get her attention.

00:01:25.957 --> 00:01:27.397
Or even say the right thing.

00:01:27.477 --> 00:01:28.917
Well, you're in luck.

00:01:29.077 --> 00:01:31.037
I know nothing about women.

00:01:31.197 --> 00:01:32.237
But I do know that we have

00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:34.957
the most amazing
way of proposing.

00:01:35.037 --> 00:01:36.037
If we start now,

00:01:36.117 --> 00:01:37.397
-we'll be ready by dawn.
-Really?

00:01:37.477 --> 00:01:38.517
Best part,

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:40.317
(WHISPERS) it involves
a lot of reindeer.

00:01:40.437 --> 00:01:41.957
-KRISTOFF: Whoa.
-(SVEN GRUNTS)

00:01:42.357 --> 00:01:43.437
MATTIAS: Hey, back at home...

00:01:43.597 --> 00:01:45.357
Halima still over
at Hudson's Hearth?

00:01:45.477 --> 00:01:46.477
She is.

00:01:46.557 --> 00:01:48.077
Really?
She married?

00:01:48.277 --> 00:01:49.317
Mm-mm.

00:01:49.477 --> 00:01:52.477
Oh, wow. Why didn't that
make me feel better?

00:01:52.637 --> 00:01:54.277
What else do you miss?

00:01:55.077 --> 00:01:56.677
My father.

00:01:56.757 --> 00:01:58.557
He passed
long before all this.

00:01:59.997 --> 00:02:02.397
He was a great man.

00:02:02.557 --> 00:02:04.077
Built us a good life
in Arendelle.

00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:07.037
But taught me to never take
the good for granted.

00:02:07.197 --> 00:02:09.477
He'd say, "Be prepared.

00:02:09.637 --> 00:02:11.077
"Just when you think
you've found your way,

00:02:11.157 --> 00:02:13.957
"life will throw you
onto a new path."

00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:16.277
What do you do when it does?

00:02:16.437 --> 00:02:17.917
Don't give up.

00:02:17.997 --> 00:02:20.997
Take it one step
at a time and...

00:02:21.477 --> 00:02:23.917
Just do the next right thing?

00:02:24.197 --> 00:02:25.717
Yeah.

00:02:25.797 --> 00:02:26.837
-You got it.
-(GIGGLES)

00:02:30.197 --> 00:02:33.237
I wanna show you something.
May I?

00:02:33.317 --> 00:02:34.517
(WHIMPERS SOFTLY)

00:02:36.117 --> 00:02:38.557
You know air, fire,
water, and earth.

00:02:38.637 --> 00:02:39.637
ELSA: Yes.

00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:41.597
HONEYMAREN: But, look,
there's a fifth spirit...

00:02:41.757 --> 00:02:44.997
said to be a bridge between us
and the magic of nature.

00:02:45.157 --> 00:02:46.357
A fifth spirit?

00:02:46.517 --> 00:02:47.797
Some say

00:02:47.877 --> 00:02:50.397
they heard it call out
the day the Forest fell.

00:02:50.557 --> 00:02:52.237
My father heard it.

00:02:52.397 --> 00:02:54.357
Do you think
that is who's calling me?

00:02:54.717 --> 00:02:58.997
Maybe.
Alas, only Ahtohallan knows.

00:02:59.157 --> 00:03:00.797
Ahtohallan.

00:03:02.637 --> 00:03:06.557
(SINGING) Dive down deep
into her sound

00:03:06.957 --> 00:03:11.237
BOTH: But not too far
or you'll be drowned

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:13.357
Why do lullabies
always have to have

00:03:13.437 --> 00:03:14.917
some terrible warning in them?

00:03:14.997 --> 00:03:16.877
(CHUCKLES)
I wonder that all the time.

00:03:16.957 --> 00:03:19.317
(HEAVY FOOTSTEPS THUDDING)

00:03:19.397 --> 00:03:20.597
Earth Giants.

00:03:21.397 --> 00:03:23.037
What are they doing down here?

00:03:24.197 --> 00:03:25.557
-(ALL WHIMPER)
-Shh!

00:03:25.997 --> 00:03:27.037
Hide.

00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:29.437
(PANTS)

00:03:30.277 --> 00:03:32.037
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

00:03:32.917 --> 00:03:34.517
-(OLAF GASPS)
-(CHITTERS)

00:03:35.397 --> 00:03:36.437
(SHUSHING)

00:03:36.517 --> 00:03:38.197
(GASPS) They're coming!

00:03:38.277 --> 00:03:39.637
(BLOWING)

00:03:40.597 --> 00:03:42.197
(YELPS, EXHALING)

00:03:42.277 --> 00:03:43.517
(GASPING)

00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:46.597
(SIGHS)

00:03:46.677 --> 00:03:49.077
This is why
we don't play with fire.

00:03:50.477 --> 00:03:53.717
Oh, I can't stay mad at you.
Why are you so cute?

00:03:53.797 --> 00:03:55.757
(FOOTSTEPS CONTINUE THUDDING)

00:03:55.837 --> 00:03:56.837
(GASPS)

00:04:05.037 --> 00:04:07.037
-(GRUNTS)
-(ELSA PANTING)

00:04:15.237 --> 00:04:16.397
(GASPS SOFTLY)

00:04:17.477 --> 00:04:18.877
-(GASPS)
-(ANNA SCOFFS)

00:04:19.637 --> 00:04:22.517
Please tell me you were not
about to follow them.

00:04:23.157 --> 00:04:25.397
What if I can settle them
like I did the wind and fire?

00:04:25.517 --> 00:04:27.117
Or what if they can crush you

00:04:27.197 --> 00:04:29.117
before you even get
the chance?

00:04:29.517 --> 00:04:32.917
Remember, the goal
is to find the voice...

00:04:33.077 --> 00:04:35.717
find the truth,
and get us home.

00:04:36.077 --> 00:04:38.237
(PANTING) Hey, guys.
That was close.

00:04:38.397 --> 00:04:39.677
-I know.
-(CHITTERS)

00:04:39.757 --> 00:04:42.037
The giants sensed me.
They may come back here.

00:04:42.157 --> 00:04:44.157
I don't want to put anyone
at risk again.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.757
And you're right, Anna.

00:04:45.957 --> 00:04:47.717
We've got to find the voice.

00:04:47.877 --> 00:04:48.997
We're going now.

00:04:49.157 --> 00:04:50.397
Okay. We're going.

00:04:50.557 --> 00:04:51.797
Let me just...

00:04:52.077 --> 00:04:53.437
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:04:54.197 --> 00:04:56.837
Wait.
Where are Kristoff and Sven?

00:04:56.917 --> 00:04:59.277
Oh, yeah. I think they
took off with that Ryder guy

00:04:59.357 --> 00:05:00.597
and a bunch of reindeer.

00:05:00.677 --> 00:05:01.957
-They left?
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:02.037 --> 00:05:04.397
Just left
without saying anything?

00:05:04.597 --> 00:05:06.637
Who knows the ways of men?

00:05:07.077 --> 00:05:08.077
(GASPS)

00:05:13.877 --> 00:05:16.277
Am I supposed to feel
this ridiculous?

00:05:16.597 --> 00:05:17.877
Oh, yeah. Definitely.

00:05:18.757 --> 00:05:19.797
Everyone ready?

00:05:19.877 --> 00:05:20.877
(AS REINDEER 1) Ready!

00:05:20.957 --> 00:05:22.237
(AS REINDEER 2) Uh,
I could use a rehearsal.

00:05:22.317 --> 00:05:23.317
(AS REINDEER 3)
I love love.

00:05:23.397 --> 00:05:25.157
Wait. You talk for them, too?

00:05:25.317 --> 00:05:26.317
(IN NORMAL VOICE) I do.

00:05:26.477 --> 00:05:28.117
It's like you can actually
hear what they're thinking.

00:05:28.277 --> 00:05:30.477
Yeah. And then
you just say it.

00:05:30.637 --> 00:05:32.277
And then you just say it.

00:05:32.357 --> 00:05:33.357
-(RUSTLING)
-(GASPS)

00:05:34.877 --> 00:05:36.997
-Okay. Here she comes.
-(GRUNTS)

00:05:37.077 --> 00:05:38.317
(GULPS)

00:05:38.397 --> 00:05:40.477
Princess Anna of Arendelle...

00:05:40.677 --> 00:05:44.877
my feisty, fearless,
ginger-sweet love.

00:05:45.037 --> 00:05:47.477
Will you marry me?

00:05:48.597 --> 00:05:49.717
Um...

00:05:49.797 --> 00:05:50.797
No.

00:05:51.157 --> 00:05:53.037
The princess left
with the queen.

00:05:53.197 --> 00:05:55.037
What? Wait, what? What?

00:05:55.197 --> 00:05:58.317
I wouldn't try to follow.
They're long gone.

00:05:58.477 --> 00:05:59.797
Long gone?

00:05:59.957 --> 00:06:02.397
So, yeah.

00:06:03.677 --> 00:06:06.237
Um, we're heading west
to the Lichen Meadows.

00:06:06.317 --> 00:06:07.957
You can come with us
if you want.

00:06:08.037 --> 00:06:09.157
(KRISTOFF GRUNTS SOFTLY)

00:06:10.397 --> 00:06:11.557
(SIGHS)

00:06:12.717 --> 00:06:15.717
Hey. Um...
I'm really sorry that...

00:06:15.917 --> 00:06:17.917
-No, it's fine.
-Yeah. Yep.

00:06:18.637 --> 00:06:21.797
(CLEARS THROAT) Okay, I better
go pack. You coming with?

00:06:21.877 --> 00:06:23.557
I'll just...
Yeah, I'll meet you there.

00:06:23.677 --> 00:06:25.557
Okay, uh, you know
where you're going, right?

00:06:25.677 --> 00:06:27.037
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Yep.

00:06:27.117 --> 00:06:28.317
I know the woods.

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:32.997
(SIGHS)

00:06:36.717 --> 00:06:37.797
(GRUNTS EMPATHETICALLY)

00:06:39.477 --> 00:06:40.877
(SIGHS DEEPLY)

00:06:41.517 --> 00:06:44.837
(SINGING) Reindeers
are better than people

00:06:45.397 --> 00:06:49.677
Sven, why is love so hard?

00:06:51.197 --> 00:06:53.077
You feel what you feel

00:06:53.237 --> 00:06:55.997
And those feelings are real

00:06:56.477 --> 00:06:57.917
Come on, Kristoff

00:06:58.077 --> 00:07:02.277
Let down your guard

00:07:03.637 --> 00:07:05.637
(POP BALLAD MUSIC PLAYING)

